    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There's only one actual test class (`AcceptanceTest`); `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a computed `@Transient` getter that derives the value from the owner's own fields:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getMembershipNumber() {\n       if (this.customerCode == null || this.registrationDate == null) {\n           return null;\n       }\n       return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", this.customerCode, this.registrationDate.getYear() % 100);\n   }\n   ```\n   `YY` uses `year % 100` zero-padded to two digits (e.g. `2026` \u2192 `26`, giving `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Design notes:** I made it a derived transient property rather than a persisted column because it's fully computed from the already-persisted `customerCode` and `registrationDate` (which the controller assigns on create, defaulting `registrationDate` to today when omitted). This keeps it always consistent with no DB migration across the four schema dialects, and matches the existing derived-field pattern (`displayName`, `initials`). MapStruct picks up the getter for `toOwnerDto` with no mapper change needed.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
